\subsection{Selective Gradient Stopping}
\label{sec:sgs_method}

To identify which gradient pathway through $e_{\Delta t}$ drives CIVO, we introduce \textit{selective gradient stopping} (SGS): during the backward pass, $e_{\Delta t}$ is detached before entering selected prediction heads via the stop-gradient operator $\operatorname{sg}(\cdot)$, preventing those loss gradients from updating $e_{\Delta t}$'s parameters while preserving its forward-pass contribution.

We test two variants. \textbf{Reward-only SGS} (exp\_016e) detaches $e_{\Delta t}$ from the reward head only: $\hat{r}_t = f_{\text{reward}}(\operatorname{sg}(e_{\Delta t}), h_t, z_t)$, testing the hypothesis that reward-loss gradients are the primary CIVO amplifier. \textbf{Full-pathway SGS} (exp\_018) detaches $e_{\Delta t}$ from all non-KL gradient pathways---observation decoders, reward head, and continuation predictor---retaining only the KL dynamics loss signal. To quantify each pathway's contribution, we perform gradient decomposition using \texttt{torch.autograd.grad}, measuring the $\ell_2$ norm of $\nabla_\theta \mathcal{L}_i$ for each loss component $\mathcal{L}_i$, where $\theta$ denotes the temporal embedding parameters.

\subsection{Environment and Training Details}
\label{sec:env_details}

All experiments use Walker Walk and Cheetah Run from the DeepMind Control Suite \citep{tassa2018dmcontrol} with proprioceptive observations. The baseline runs for 500K environment steps, sufficient for convergence (peak return 970.4 on Walker Walk). Treatment configurations run for 105K steps, which is sufficient to observe both collapse onset and the diagnostic markers described above. All DreamerV3 hyperparameters follow the defaults from \citet{hafner2023dreamerv3} without task-specific tuning. Training uses a single NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada GPU with JIT compilation disabled (\texttt{-{}-compile False}) for reproducibility across runs. The codebase extends DreamerV3 with the variable-rate modules described in \S\ref{sec:variable_rate}; no other architectural modifications are made.

